<title>AUSTRALIA: BHP guarded about Foster's stake.</title>
<headline>BHP guarded about Foster's stake.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd managing director John Prescott said on Tuesday the company believed that its first priority with Foster's Brewing Group Ltd was to improve the beer maker's performance.</p>
<p>Prescott, asked at a news conference about the future of non-core assets, did not say if BHP planned to sell its 36 percent stake in the near future as has been speculated by a number of analysts and newspapers in recent months.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a whole range of priorities. The first priority I think with Foster's is to improve the performance of Foster's.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
